# JsonApiPoc request collection — index.
#
# The requests live in Http/, one file per endpoint group:
#
#   Http/Companies.http     /api/companies      list, single, and the contacts related collection
#   Http/Contacts.http      /api/contacts       list, single, company relationship, writes
#   Http/Deals.http         /api/deals          list, single, three relationships, writes
#   Http/Activities.http    /api/activities     list, single, deal and contact relationships
#   Http/Users.http         /api/users          list, single
#   Http/CustomFields.http  /api/custom-fields  the tenant-defined field catalog
#
# How those files work (Rider / VS 2022 / VS Code "REST Client" extension):
#   - `@name = value` defines a file-level variable; `{{name}}` interpolates it into requests.
#   - `###` starts a new request; everything until the next `###` is one request:
#     method + URL, then headers, then a blank line, then an optional body.
#   - Lines starting with # or // are comments; the text after ### becomes the request's name.
#   - Click the "run" icon in the editor gutter (or Ctrl+Alt+Enter in VS Code) to send one.
#   - The expected outcome of each request is noted after "->" in its title.
#
# Start the API first:  dotnet run --project JsonApiPoc
# Interactive docs:     http://localhost:5031/swagger

@host = http://localhost:5031

### Smoke test: the API is up
GET {{host}}/api/companies
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
